## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                   ← builds the Express app; separate from main.ts so tests can import it directly
├── config/env.ts             ← the only file that reads process.env
├── errors/app-error.ts       ← AppError, NotFoundError, ValidationError
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← shared kernel: database clients, cache, auth, health checks
└── modules/<module>/
    ├── index.ts              ← **public API barrel** — exports ONLY the service class
    ├── <module>.entity.ts    ← the model{{#if ormTypeorm}} (also the TypeORM persistence entity){{/if}}
    ├── <module>.repository.ts ← data access (branched by ORM)
    ├── <module>.service.ts   ← business logic
    ├── <module>.controller.ts ← Express req/res handlers
    ├── <module>.routes.ts    ← wires repository → service → controller → router (manual, no DI container)
    ├── dto/
    │   └── create-<module>.dto.ts ← request body validation
    └── <module>.service.spec.ts   ← unit tests for the service
```

### Module rules

- **`index.ts` is the public API.** It exports only the service class. Nothing else.
- **Modules only import from other modules' `index.ts`**. No internal cross-imports.
- **`shared/` is the shared kernel.** Common infra used by more than one module.
- **`routes.ts` is the composition root.** Manual wiring, no DI.

Call direction inside a module: `routes` wires everything → `controller` → `service` → `repository`. Cross-module: `service A` → `index.ts of module B` → `service B`.

